-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura: local anemic Hecke algebra as a corner ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \neq 0$, a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ containing every prime divisor of $N$, and a further natural number $r$; let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring which is a domain, complete for its maximal ideal, with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, and assume (as a `Fact`) [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), i.e. that the integral lattice [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spans $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ over $\mathbb{C}$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$, to $k$, and let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (insert r S)`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $k$ which, by hypothesis, is $\theta$ composed with the inclusion of the smaller anemic algebra `heckeAlgebra N 2 (insert r S)` into `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` supplied by [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra_mono`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L45). Assume [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.BaseOpComm N r S 𝒪`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleBase.html#L14): the operators `baseOp N r S 𝒪 g`, indexed by $g \in$ [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.Gen N r S`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModule.html#L11) (a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \neq r$), commute pairwise in $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1(N,\top;\mathcal{O}))$; these operators, together with $g \mapsto \theta(T_\ell)$, form the Hecke datum [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.baseHeckeData N r S 𝒪 θ hc₀`](def/CuspForm_AuxLevelHeckeModuleBase.html#L17), whose `opSubalgebra` is the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra $B$ of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1(N,\top;\mathcal{O}))$ generated by the range of these operators. Assume further a non-Eisenstein condition: there is a prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \neq r$, $\ell \equiv 1 \pmod{N}$ and $\theta(T_\ell) \neq \ell + 1$ in $k$. Finally let $Sp$ be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of $B$, that is, an integer $n$, complete orthogonal idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_0,\dots,\mathfrak{m}_{n-1}$ of $B$ exhausting the maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly when $i \neq j$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$ to $k$ sending $e_{i_0}(\mathrm{baseOp}\,g)e_{i_0}$ to $\theta(T_{\ell_g})$ for every generator $g$, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N (insert r S) 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) onto that corner ring which carries the image under the canonical map [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) of $T_{\ell_g}$ (for $\ell_g \notin \{r\} \cup S$) to $e_{i_0}(\mathrm{baseOp}\,g)e_{i_0}$, for every $g$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura comparison in its anemic form: away from a finite set of primes containing those dividing the level, the local weight-two Hecke algebra of $\Gamma_0(N)$ at a non-Eisenstein residual eigensystem is identified, compatibly with the Hecke operators $T_\ell$, with a corner ring of the algebra generated by the corresponding operators on the degree-one cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $\mathcal{O}$-coefficients. It is invoked by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_moduleEnd_baseML_injective`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algHom_moduleEnd_baseML_injective) to make the local Hecke algebra act faithfully on the localised cohomology used in the Taylor–Wiles argument.
